:R-HSA-933542  a            obo:GO_0008150 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "The TRAF6/TAK1 signal activates a canonical IKK complex, resulting in the activation of NF-kB as well as MAPK cascades leading to the activation of AP-1. Although TRAF6/TAK1 has been implicated in Tool like receptor (TLR) mediated cytokine production, the involvement of these molecules in the regulation of type I IFN induction mediated by RIG-I/MDA5 pathway is largely unknown. According to the study done by Yoshida et al RIG-I/IPS-1 pathway requires TRAF6 and MAP3K, MEKK1 to activate NF-kB and MAP Kinases for optimal induction of type I IFNs." ;
        rdfs:label          "TRAF6 mediated NF-kB activation" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" , "Reviewed: Kawai, T, Akira, S, 2010-10-30" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Edited: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-933542" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-168928/R-HSA-168928> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

